WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:06.517
There's a trend in many industries
to face a lot of new challenges,

00:00:06.517 --> 00:00:10.218
every industry now is either undergoing or

00:00:10.218 --> 00:00:14.662
is seeing the threat or
the promise of disruption.

00:00:14.662 --> 00:00:18.070
[MUSIC]

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:24.035
This program is all about
delivering value for your company.

00:00:24.035 --> 00:00:30.170
Getting the mechanisms to actually
drive innovation in your organization.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.591
&gt;&gt; The big challenge I think, is figuring
out how to innovate at large corporations.

00:00:33.591 --> 00:00:36.220
It's exactly what this
program was geared around.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.929
So it felt like it was a perfect fit.

00:00:37.929 --> 00:00:41.122
&gt;&gt; The program actually brings
together three strengths of

00:00:41.122 --> 00:00:43.800
the Stanford Graduate School of Business.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.260
The first one is really our expertise
in creating new businesses.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:52.878
The second one is our expertise in
innovation in large organization,

00:00:52.878 --> 00:00:55.040
in a corporate setting.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.315
And the third one is all about
the idea of organizational change.

00:00:59.315 --> 00:01:04.580
&gt;&gt; I found the two companies and
now I'm at a big corporate company.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:08.016
The program is ideally suited
because it links the two, right?

00:01:08.016 --> 00:01:14.410
My entrepreneurial spirit with the
sometimes obstacles in big corporations.

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:18.265
&gt;&gt; I was looking for something that
would really lead me towards innovation,

00:01:18.265 --> 00:01:22.133
I really found that the structure of this
program was going to be ideal for me.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:25.380
&gt;&gt; My role is to be
the corporate entrepreneur.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.154
And I often find myself in
a place where nobody gets or

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.750
understands what I'm thinking or
trying to do.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.117
And so I wanted to find a place where I
belonged, and that I could associate with

00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:39.160
other people who were thinking
in similar patterns to me.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.626
&gt;&gt; The project component makes it
an experiential learning in a much more

00:01:43.626 --> 00:01:45.906
effective practical experience.

00:01:45.906 --> 00:01:51.170
These are real projects,
our participants bring in the project.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:54.258
Some of the projects
become the way to learn.

00:01:54.258 --> 00:01:59.730
By going through a real project and
working on it and developing it.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:03.923
We see the content from the classroom
actually being applied in a real

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:07.043
life setting,
where a lot of the learning occurs.

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:09.911
&gt;&gt; The experiential aspect
was extremely important, and

00:02:09.911 --> 00:02:12.970
that's what sets this program
apart from other programs.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.672
You get to live what you learn,
and see if it actually works,

00:02:16.672 --> 00:02:18.641
and see if you can execute on it.

00:02:18.641 --> 00:02:22.690
&gt;&gt; The cohort is fabulous,
we have people from all around the world.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:26.469
We're all this corporate entrepreneur who
feel that the rest of the organisation

00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:27.628
doesn't always get us.

00:02:27.628 --> 00:02:32.590
And some people get us but not everybody,
and that we're in this thing together.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:36.674
&gt;&gt; You're surrounded by people
who have very similar issues.

00:02:36.674 --> 00:02:39.531
You learn a lot from
the experience of others, but

00:02:39.531 --> 00:02:43.683
it also becomes sort of a support
group for the corporate entrepreneur,

00:02:43.683 --> 00:02:47.580
which creates long lasting networks
that are useful in the future.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.860
&gt;&gt; The world is turning faster.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:55.280
Even Google now has to take care to
keep the speed and keep the innovation.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.633
You need a constant rethinking of
your ideas of new business models,

00:02:59.633 --> 00:03:01.215
a constant innovation.

00:03:01.215 --> 00:03:07.026
&gt;&gt; The program helps you take an idea and
develop it, evaluate it,

00:03:07.026 --> 00:03:12.634
communicate it, and
finally have the tools to execute on it.

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:16.138
[MUSIC]

